                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "asymptotes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29b76317-4f09-338d-b611-3fe14dee0206",
                        "entry_id": "6153e64f-fdd1-3a58-8e38-b86ac92b0daa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A straight line which a curve approaches arbitrarily closely as it goes to infinity. The limit of the curve; its tangent \\\"at infinity\\\"."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f57311be-32dd-4975-a1ae-8d90b6da5e2f",
                                "sense_id": "29b76317-4f09-338d-b611-3fe14dee0206",
                                "text": "The King rushed forward with all his cruel coordinates and mean values, stumbled into a dark forest of roots and logarithms, had to backtrack, then encountered the beast on a field of irrational numbers (F₁) and smote it so grievously that it fell two decimal places and lost an epsilon, but the beast slid around an asymptote and hid in an n-dimensional orthogonal phase space, underwent expansion and came out, fuming factorially, and fell upon the King and hurt him passing sore."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa2889a0-5718-3974-ad53-dcab3a722f57",
                        "entry_id": "6153e64f-fdd1-3a58-8e38-b86ac92b0daa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Anything which comes near to but never meets something else."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a8b5edf-e6c9-4184-9071-c0a8196b59c3",
                                "sense_id": "fa2889a0-5718-3974-ad53-dcab3a722f57",
                                "text": "Language, in relation to thought, must ever be regarded as an asymptote."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
